(Abstract) Tj T*
/F2 10 Tf
14 TL
(Background: The influence of lifestyle factors on cognitive health, particularly among ) Tj T*
(middle-aged and older adults, has garnered significant attention in gerontology and cognitive ) Tj T*
(neuroscience. Currently, over 55 million people worldwide are living with dementia, including ) Tj T*
(Alzheimer's disease with nearly 10 million new cases annually. Although sedentary behavior has ) Tj T*
(been associated with cognitive decline, these studies often treat sitting time as a ) Tj T*
(homogeneous entity, without considering the specific nature of sedentary activities. | ) Tj T*
(Objective: This systematic review aims to examine associations of individual sitting ) Tj T*
(activities with cognitive function in middle-aged and older adults. | Methods: Data were ) Tj T*
(searched using eight electronic databases \(EMBASE, Web of Science, PsycINFO, CINAHL, Medline, ) Tj T*
(SPORTDiscus, PubMed, and Scopus\) from inception to September 2024. Qualitative studies, ) Tj T*
(reviews, conference abstracts, theses, and book chapters were excluded. The methodological ) Tj T*
(quality of included studies was assessed using the QualSyst tool. | Results: A total of 85 ) Tj T*
(studies \(n = 1,575,657\) were included in this review. Of the 43 studies examining television ) Tj T*
(viewing, 28 \(65%\) reported a negative association between prolonged television viewing and ) Tj T*
(cognitive function. Conversely, among the 58 studies that included active sedentary ) Tj T*
(activities, only five \(8.6%\) reported negative associations. | Conclusions: The cognitive ) Tj T*
(effects of sedentary behavior depend on the type of activity performed. Promoting cognitively ) Tj T*
(engaging sedentary activities may support healthy cognitive aging, while excessive passive ) Tj T*
(behaviors may increase risk of cognitive decline and Alzheimer's disease. Future research ) Tj T*
(should focus on further clarifying the mechanisms behind these associations and explore ) Tj T*
(interventions to enhance cognitive health in aging populations.) Tj T*
